@startuml
title SYS01 - Queueing deploy, rollback and automatic recovery

actor Scheduler
actor Operator
participant "Deployment workflow (deploy.yml)" as Workflow
participant "DEI VM deploy agent" as Deploy
database "Shared DEI PostgreSQL 18" as DEIDB
participant "GitHub artifacts" as Artifacts

Scheduler -> Workflow: Scheduled deploy run A
Workflow -> Workflow: Enter `dei-release` queue; acquire exclusive slot
Workflow -> Deploy: Deploy candidate under VM lock
Deploy -> DEIDB: Candidate app uses current schema
DEIDB --> Deploy: Connection succeeds
Deploy --> Workflow: Post-deploy smoke test fails
Workflow -> Deploy: Automatic recovery to previous release
Deploy -> DEIDB: Previous app compatibility smoke check
DEIDB --> Deploy: Previous release is restored and verified

Operator -> Workflow: Manual rollback run B arrives during recovery
Workflow -> Workflow: Queue run B; it cannot acquire slot yet
Workflow -> Artifacts: Archive run A failure and recovery evidence
Workflow -> Workflow: Finish run A; release `dei-release` slot

Workflow -> Workflow: Start run B; acquire same exclusive slot
Workflow -> Deploy: Re-read active manifest/schema; run rollback eligibility checks
alt Requested release remains retained and schema-compatible
  Deploy --> Workflow: Eligibility confirmed
  Workflow -> Deploy: Activate requested release under VM lock
  Deploy --> Workflow: Smoke checks pass
  Workflow -> Artifacts: Archive run B recovery evidence
  Workflow --> Operator: Rollback complete; release queue slot
else Requested release is not schema-compatible
  Deploy --> Workflow: Reject before changing VM
  Workflow -> Artifacts: Archive sanitized rejection
  Workflow --> Operator: No activation; release queue slot
end

note over Workflow,Deploy
  Workflow concurrency is `group: dei-release`, `queue: max`,
  so up to 100 runs wait rather than replacing a pending run.
  Only one operation mutates the VM at a time. Automatic recovery
  remains inside run A and holds its slot. A VM-side lock is a second guard.
  The independent main.yml CI workflow does not touch this queue or VM.
end note
@enduml
